				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				23
			],
			"Message": "test(Maintain): split integration tests into Syntactic and Integration suites\n\nSplit the original Eliminate integration tests into two binary-compatible\nsuites: Syntactic (for fast, string-based comparison) and Integration\n(for semantically-validating via rustc).  The integration suite now compiles\ntransformed snippets to validate semantic equivalence.\n\nThis separation allows for faster, more targeted testing of the elimination\nlogic (syntactic) versus real-world usage (integration) and improves\nmaintainability by modularising the test files.\n\nRename `tests/Eliminate.rs` → `tests/Eliminate/Syntactic.rs` and\nintroduce `tests/Eliminate/Integration.rs` with per-test files under\n`tests/Eliminate/Integration/`.  Both test suites are built by `cargo test`.",
			"SHA": "ad03561e6603ff1f089e8e4fa4859c9a2ad3f24c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-24T15:55:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "test(Maintain): Add comprehensive test cases for Eliminate pass transformations\n\nExpand test coverage in `tests/Eliminate.rs` with detailed assertions for expression inlining, macro handling, and real-world Mountain backend patterns. Key additions include:\n\n- Cast expression handling (`CastExprInlined`, `CastExprNeedsParen`)\n- JSON macro token handling (`DerefOnceLockIntoJsonMacro`, `TypeAnnotatedCollectIntoJsonMacro`)\n- Closure-local binding inlining (`ClosureLocalBindingsInlined`)\n- Match scrutinee inlining (`OptionBindingIntoMatchScrutinee`, `ChainIntoMatchDiscriminant`)\n- Async inlining patterns with `tokio::fs` and `json!` macro use\n- Safety assertions for multi-use variables and pre-clone handling (`RangeDoubleBoundKept`, `PreCloneForMoveClosureKept`)\n\nThese test cases validate the `Eliminate` transformer's behavior in complex expression contexts, including real-world patterns from the Mountain backend.",
			"SHA": "eaa6a54c54224b010bbef7a8bfb2b892e96bf48f"
		}
